  TJJM gym-website overrides, file 5. Same format as files 1-4: ~Name|URL~
  An EMPTY value blanks the link. Only add an entry that CHANGES something.
  Rendered after file 4 by BOTH sections. Gate C3 forbids a name in two files.

  16 Aug 2026 - BATCH 37. FALSE-POSITIVE RESTORATIONS, moved out of tjjm-gym-websites.liquid.

  131 records blanked for a dead-or-unreachable reason were re-tested on BOTH the apex and the
  www form, then opened and read. 21 were live schools we had wrongly un-linked - a 16%
  false-positive rate. Eleven of them lived in file 1, which had only 544 bytes of headroom, so
  their blanking rows were DELETED there and rewritten here with the working URL. Gate C3 stays
  intact: each of those names now appears in exactly one override file, this one.

  ROOT CAUSE: every screen tested the hostname EXACTLY AS STORED. A domain can be NXDOMAIN on
  www.foo.com while foo.com is alive and serving the school. Four of the first eight false
  positives were exactly that. NEW RULE: a domain is dead only if BOTH forms fail.

  SECOND FINDING, worse: the fetcher used by most screens serves STALE CACHED page bodies, not
  just cached copies of NXDOMAIN domains. Six domains returned live-looking school content to a
  fetch that a real browser showed were dead. Any verdict resting on a fetched body rather than
  a browser load is softer evidence than it looked. Detail in
  CRITICAL-false-positive-removals.md.

  Where a record had BOTH an alt-form hit and a batch-36 search recovery, the RECOVERY URL WON:
  it is name-matched and city-confirmed. Hence ONE HEART DOJO -> oneheartdojo.net rather than
  eldoradomartialarts.com; Martial Arts America Russellville -> russellvillemaa.com rather than
  a taekwondo domain whose body would not load; Port City Combat Sports -> its Fairhope page
  rather than the Mobile AL address the alt-form check landed on.
